deepseek_plan rep0 27/48 3hop1__79039_131926_90707: 'The question asks: "Where does that body of water meet the Ohio River?"\n\nWe need to identify which body of water meets the Ohio River based on the provided passages.\n\nLooking through the passages:\n\n- The Beaurivage River flows into the Chaudière River — not the Ohio River.\n- Silver Lake (Madison, NH) flows to the Saco River — not the Ohio River.\n- Proctorville is along the Ohio River — but not a body of water meeting it.\n- The Hocking River is a tributary of the Ohio River — so it flows into the Ohio River.\n- The Kentucky River is a tributary of the Ohio River — so it flows into the Ohio River.\n- The Allegheny River joins the Monongahela River to form the Ohio River — so it meets the Ohio River.\n- The Ohio River itself flows into the Mississippi River — not the meeting point of another body of water.\n- Powwow Pond flows to the Merrimack River — not the Ohio River.\n- Contoocook Lake feeds into the Contoocook River, which flows to the Merrimack River — not the Ohio River.\n- Silver Lake (Harrisville, NH) flows to the Ashuelot River — not the Ohio River.\n- The Ekulu River is in Nigeria — not related.\n- Davis Island Lock and Dam Site pumps water from the Ohio River — not a meeting point.\n- Mamaroneck River flows into Long Island Sound — not the Ohio River.\n- Jucy Lucy is a burger — irrelevant.\n\nNow, which of these bodies of water actually "meet" the Ohio River?\n\n- The Hocking River is a right tributary of the Ohio River → it meets the Ohio River.\n- The Kentucky River is a tributary of the Ohio River → it meets the Ohio River.\n- The Allegheny River joins the Monongahela River to form the Ohio River → it meets the Ohio River at Pittsburgh.\n\nSo multiple bodies of water meet the Ohio River. But the question is: "Where does that body of water meet the Ohio River?"\n\nThe phrasing "that body of water" implies a specific one, but no specific body of water is named in the question. However, the only passage that explicitly describes a body of water meeting the Ohio River is the Allegheny River, which forms the Ohio River at Pittsburgh.\n\nBut the question is not asking "which body of water meets the Ohio River?" — it\'s asking "where does that body of water meet the Ohio River?"\n\nSo we need to find the location where a body of water meets the Ohio River.\n\nFrom passage 10: "The Allegheny River joins with the Monongahela River to form the Ohio River at the \'Point\' of Point State Park in Downtown Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania."\n\nSo the Allegheny River meets the Ohio River at Pittsburgh, Pennsylvania.\n\nSimilarly, the Kentucky River flows into the Ohio River in Kentucky — but no specific location is given.\n\nThe Hocking River is in southeastern Ohio — but no meeting point is specified.\n\nOnly the Allegheny River has a specific meeting point:' (gold 'at the city of Cairo, Illinois')
