small_plan rep0 38/48 4hop1__749363_49925_13759_736921: 'The question asks for the state where the district where the man who wanted to reform the religion practiced by Innocenzo Ferrieri preached a sermon on Marian devotion is located.\n\nStep 1: Identify who "the man who wanted to reform the religion practiced by Innocenzo Ferrieri" is.\n\nInnocenzo Ferrieri was an Italian cardinal of the Roman Catholic Church. The passage about him (idx=2) does not mention any reformer associated with him. However, the passage about Pope Paul VI (idx=17) mentions that he was a Marian devotee and spoke at Marian congresses and meetings, visited Marian shrines, and issued Marian encyclicals. He also re-convened the Second Vatican Council and promoted reform in the Church.\n\nThe passage about Ambroise-Marie Carré (idx=14) mentions that he preached sermons at Notre Dame de Paris and was called to present spiritual exercises at the Vatican. He also preached Lenten sermons many times at Notre Dame de Paris.\n\nBut the key point is that the question is about a man who wanted to reform the religion practiced by Innocenzo Ferrieri — i.e., the Roman Catholic Church. Among the passages, Pope Paul VI is explicitly described as a reformer of the Church, and he is a Marian devotee.\n\nStep 2: Where did Pope Paul VI preach sermons on Marian devotion?\n\nThe passage about Pope Paul VI (idx=17) says: "He preached the Lenten sermons many times at Notre Dame de Paris" — this is not directly about Marian devotion, but it is a sermon at Notre Dame de Paris.\n\nHowever, the passage about Ambroise-Marie Carré (idx=14) says: "He preached the Lenten sermons many times at Notre Dame de Paris, and in 1964, Paul VI called him to present spiritual exercises at the Vatican."\n\nThis suggests that Ambroise-Marie Carré was active in France and preached in Paris.\n\nBut the question is about the man who wanted to reform the religion practiced by Innocenzo Ferrieri — that is, the Catholic Church. The only person described as a reformer in the Catholic Church in the passages is Pope Paul VI.\n\nBut the passage about Pope Paul VI (idx=17) does not say where he preached on Marian devotion specifically.\n\nThe passage about Henry Scott Holland (idx=13) says: "While at St Paul\'s Cathedral Holland delivered a sermon in May 1910... titled Death the King of Terrors... from his discussion of the latter that perhaps his best-known writing, Death is nothing at all, is drawn." This is about death, not Marian devotion.\n\nThe passage about Martin Luther (idx=1) discusses his views on Marian devotion, but not where he preached.\n\nThe passage about Ambroise-Marie Carré (idx=14) says he preached sermons in France and abroad — especially in the Netherlands, Switzerland, Italy, and Belgium — and at Notre Dame de Paris.\n\nBut there is no mention of a sermon on Marian devotion by any of these' (gold 'Saxony-Anhalt')
